METHOD: re-extracted the CURRENT <script> block from accounts.html (not the
old S4 extraction) into a fresh Node/vm harness that loads the DOM in the
correct order (elements exist before the script runs, matching real parse
order -- the old harness had a bug where `region` was captured before the
DOM existed and every write silently went to a detached global; fixed via
vm.createContext per "page load"), then independently reproduced both
sequences in a REAL Chromium browser (Playwright 1.62.1, playwright-core
already vendored under scratchpad/pw) against a built server
(go build ./cmd/server) on an isolated data dir
(scratchpad/cs2/data, :18491) with two accounts whose patterns genuinely
overlap a real CSV, plus CDP Accessibility.getFullAXTree, matching
judge-claude's S4.3 method.

1) SEQUENCE 1 (dismiss -> overlap resolved by a real edit -> SAME overlap
recreated by a real edit) -- FIXED. Real browser, real HTMX form submits:
  load:      region=warning text, banner=true, dismissBtn=true, storedKey=null
  dismiss:   region="Pattern overlap warning dismissed.", banner=false, storedKey=<key>
  resolved:  region unchanged (empty-content guard), banner=false, storedKey=null  <- cleared
  recreated: region=warning text, banner=true, dismissBtn=true, storedKey=null
Banner and region agree at every step; the S4 defect (region asserting an
active warning with no banner/dismiss control) does not reproduce.

2) SEQUENCE 2 (dismiss -> ordinary reload, warnings unchanged) -- FIXED.
Real browser:
  after dismiss+reload: region.textContent = "", banner absent.
  CDP getFullAXTree: 0 un-ignored nodes containing "Pattern overlap warning".
This is exactly what judge-claude's S4.3 verdict said would change the
ruling ("If the sr-only region had been empty ... after dismiss+reload,
sequence 2 would collapse"). It is empty.

3) Root-cause mechanism (whitespace-padded region vs unpadded
data-warnings-text defeating the same-text guard on every load) -- FIXED.
Server-rendered region markup is now single-line (curl'd raw bytes: no
leading/trailing whitespace inside the div). A document-wide
MutationObserver installed via addInitScript before the page's own script,
across two consecutive full loads with warnings unchanged and no
dismissal, recorded zero mutations on #accounts-warnings-region on either
load.

4) Reworded confirmation + scoped test (item c) -- verified, not just read.
scriptBlockRE = `(?s)<script[^>]*>.*?</script>` strips every <script> block
(checked: no literal "</script" substring appears inside any script body in
accounts.html or base.html, so the non-greedy match can't truncate early);
"Pattern overlap warning" does not appear anywhere outside a script tag when
Warnings is empty (both string- and attribute-guarded by {{if .Warnings}}).
Ran the actual tests: TestHandlePage_RendererMode_NoOverlapRendersNoWarningBlock
and TestHandlePage_RendererMode_OverlapRendersWarningBlockOnce both PASS.

5) Item (b) TestWarningsKey_OrderInvariant -- verified the mutation-guard
actually guards: asserts on `b` (unsorted input, ["b","a"]), not `a` (already
sorted), so an in-place sort would be caught. PASS.

6) Item (d) describeAlreadyResolved load-failure branch -- traced the call
path: DataLoader.suspectedIdentities is a purely in-memory scan of
dl.suspectedTransfers; it never touches transfer_decisions.json. So
ResolveTransfer("whatever-key", ...) with an unseeded queue fails fast
in-memory ("no suspected transfer pair with key"), routing the handler into
describeAlreadyResolved, which is the function that DOES call
LoadTransferDecisions() against the corrupted file. The test genuinely
reaches the load-failure branch, not the unknown-key branch of that
function. go test -run confirms PASS.

7) Item (e) comment -- internal/services/accounts/projection_test.go's
TestProject_MixedRecurringFiltersByAccount comment now names
recurringOwnerAccount (current) instead of the deleted
recurringBelongsToAccount, and matches the tie-break the test actually
exercises.

HYPOTHESIS I RAISED AND THEN DISPROVED (reporting for the record, not as a
finding): a mutation handler's renderError() (accounts/handlers.go) writes a
bare error <div> with status 400/404/500 and no accounts-warnings-data node,
and every form in accounts.html targets hx-target="#accounts-list". I
reasoned a race (e.g. double-clicking "Delete" on an anchor) could make
htmx swap that bare error card into #accounts-list, destroying
#accounts-warnings-data and the banner while leaving
#accounts-warnings-region stale -- syncWarnings' `if (!data) return` would
never run to clear it, a live point-16 violation. I built this in a Node
harness and it "reproduced" there. I then drove the ACTUAL failure through a
real browser against the real server (raced two genuine POSTs to the same
anchor-delete endpoint, confirmed server-side that the second really is a
404) and, critically, drove it through htmx's real client, not raw fetch:
base.html's htmx:beforeSwap handler only forces a swap on 4xx when the
response carries an HX-Retarget header, which accounts' renderError never
sets, so htmx 2.0.4's default (no swap on non-2xx without that header)
applies. Confirmed with page.evaluate(() => form.requestSubmit();
form.requestSubmit()) on the live anchor-delete form: final DOM after both
responses land reflects ONLY the first (successful) response's swap; the
404 body never reaches #accounts-list, #accounts-warnings-data survives,
and the region is untouched-but-correct. This branch of syncWarnings
(missing-data-node) is therefore dead in production for accounts and not a
live defect. Recording this so the next checker doesn't have to re-walk it.

NON-BLOCKING OBSERVATION (not filed as a defect): the sessionStorage
dismissal key is single-slot and content-keyed, not history-stacked. Dismiss
warning-set W1 (key K1) -> a DIFFERENT overlap W2 (key K2) appears and is
correctly shown/announced -> W1 (K1) reappears unchanged: it comes back
suppressed (region empty, banner absent) with no independent dismissal for
that reappearance, because storedKey is only cleared when the CURRENT key is
empty (S5's fix), not when it changes to a different non-empty key.
Confirmed via harness. This does not violate point 16 as written --
banner and region stay in lockstep the whole time, so there is no channel
divergence -- and the single-slot, content-keyed design is inherited from
S3/S4, explicitly defended in the code's own comments, and outside
REVIEW_AUG20_SPEC.md's S5 row (a), which is scoped to the
`if (!banner) return` early-return bug. Flagging for the record in case a
future point extends "state change" to cover this case explicitly.

sessionStorage-throws path (Safari private mode) reasoned through against
the source: getItem/setItem/removeItem are each individually try/caught;
a throw on read defaults dismissed=false (warning stays visible, not
stuck hidden); a throw on write during dismiss still hides the banner and
writes the confirmation for THIS render (the two statements after the
setItem try/catch are unconditional), but the dismissal does not persist,
so the NEXT load/swap shows the warning again -- degraded, not stuck.

go build ./... and go vet ./... clean; go test ./... green repo-wide
(only budget2/web has no test files, unrelated).

No sequence, ordering, or state I could construct broke S5's specific
claims or ACCESSIBILITY.md point 16 as written. PASS.
